issue_context.body:
### What did you do?

1. Configure remote read in Prometheus.
2. Issue a large number of queries that trigger remote read.
```
up{job="cloudwatch",la=~"va",lb!~"vb",debug="true"}
```

### What did you expect to see?

The label matchers specified in the original query should be consistently applied in the remote read request. Even when a large number of queries are issued, the same matchers should be applied consistently across all remote read requests.

### What did you see instead? Under which circumstances?

Occasionally, the order of the label matchers changes, or some label matchers are missing from the remote read request.

### System information

Linux 5.15.0-1067-aws x86_64

### Prometheus version

```text
$ /usr/local/prometheus/bin/prometheus --version
prometheus, version 2.53.2 (branch: HEAD, revision: 6e971a7dc905696d4bc4ffa150bf282fcfac5fa9)
  build user:       root@363b0aa99939
  build date:       20240809-14:55:04
  go version:       go1.22.6
  platform:         linux/amd64
  tags:             netgo,builtinassets,stringlabels
```


### Prometheus configuration file

```yaml
remote_read:
  - url: http://localhost:9415/read
    read_recent: true
    required_matchers:
      job: cloudwatch
```


### Alertmanager version

_No response_

### Alertmanager configuration file

_No response_

### Logs
To isolate the cause, I used a tool called bpftrace to investigate the parameters being passed during remote read requests.

Prepare bpftrace and script.
The script dump query at https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/blob/v2.53.2/storage/remote/client.go#L276 .
```text
$ wget https://github.com/bpftrace/bpftrace/releases/download/v0.20.4/bpftrace
$ cat trace.bt
struct GoString {
  char* str;
  int64_t len;
}

struct LabelMatcher {
  int32_t Type;
  char padding[4];
  struct GoString Name;
  struct GoString Value;
}

struct LabelMatcherSlice {
  struct LabelMatcher** items; // array
  int64_t len;
  int64_t cap;
}

struct Query {
  int64_t StartTimestampMs;
  int64_t EndTimestampMs;
  struct LabelMatcherSlice Matchers;
  void* Hints;
}

uprobe:/usr/local/prometheus/bin/prometheus:"github.com/prometheus/prometheus/storage/remote.(*Client).Read"
{
    $query = (struct Query *) (reg("di"));

    $target = false;
    $i = 0; $max = $query->Matchers.len; if ($max > 10) { $max = 10; }
    while ($i < $max) {
      $name = str((*($query->Matchers.items+$i))->Name.str, (*($query->Matchers.items+$i))->Name.len);
      if ($name == "debug") {
        $target = true;
      }
      $i++;
    }

    if ($target) {
      printf("%d: ", $query->Matchers.len);
      $i = 0; $max = $query->Matchers.len; if ($max > 10) { $max = 10;}
      while ($i < $max) {
        $type = (*($query->Matchers.items+$i))->Type;
        $e = "=";
        if ($type == 1) {
          $e = "!=";
        } else if ($type == 2) {
          $e = "=~";
        } else if ($type == 3) {
          $e = "!~";
        }
        $name = str((*($query->Matchers.items+$i))->Name.str, (*($query->Matchers.items+$i))->Name.len);
        $value = str((*($query->Matchers.items+$i))->Value.str, (*($query->Matchers.items+$i))->Value.len);
        printf("%s%s\"%s\",", $name, $e, $value);
        $i++;
      }
      printf("\n");
    }
}
```

Run bpftrace.
```
$ sudo ./bpftrace -p $(pgrep -f 'bin/prometheus .*prometheus.yml') trace.bt | tee trace.log
Attaching 1 probe...
```

Issue a large number of queries.
```
$ for i in $(seq 1 5000); do curl -s 'http://localhost:9090/prometheus/api/v1/query?query=up%7Bjob%3D%22cloudwatch%22%2Cla%3D~%22va%22%2Clb%21~%22vb%22%2Cdebug%3D%22true%22%7D&time=2024-08-20T00:00:00.000Z' > /dev/null; done
```

I confirmed that the label matchers are inconsistent.
```
$ sort -u trace.log
5: job="cloudwatch",la=~"va",debug="true",__name__="up",lb!~"vb",
5: job="cloudwatch",la=~"va",debug="true",lb!~"vb",__name__="up",
5: job="cloudwatch",la=~"va",lb!~"vb",debug="true",__name__="up",
5: job="cloudwatch",la=~"va",lb!~"vb",debug="true",lb!~"vb",
Attaching 1 probe...
```
